---
description: Database safety for SQL, schema, migrations and queries (Oracle-aware).
globs: "**/*.sql,**/migrations/**,**/*.pls,**/*.pks,**/*.pkb"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Database

- Use the `database` skill (or `database` subagent) for any SQL, schema, index or migration change.
- Never execute automatically: DROP, TRUNCATE, mass DELETE/UPDATE, destructive ALTER, destructive migrations.
  Flow: ANALYZE -> GENERATE SCRIPT -> SHOW IMPACT (rows, locks, rollback) -> HUMAN APPROVAL -> EXECUTE.
- Bind variables / parameterized queries always; never build SQL by string concatenation with external input.
- Migrations ship a forward and a rollback script; prefer expand -> migrate -> contract for compatibility.
- Oracle: DDL auto-commits (no transactional rollback); statements about optimizer/plan behavior must come from a real
  execution plan (`DBMS_XPLAN`) or be labelled ASSUMPTION. Never invent a plan or statistics.
- Never run against production; connection strings and credentials come from env vars, never from files in the repo.
